# FKBC Fight Arcade

Production game project for FKBC.

## Game concept

An original retro martial-arts game inspired by the gameplay principles of classic
16-bit arcade fighters and scrolling beat-'em-ups.

The game has two primary modes.

### Arcade Fight

Traditional 1-v-1 fighting.

- Joe
- Jack
- John
- Justin
- Paul

Features:

- Best-of-three rounds
- 99-second timer
- Six-button combat
- Standing, crouching and jumping attacks
- High and low blocking
- Throws
- Knockdowns and recovery
- Combos
- Special moves
- Super meter
- Projectiles
- CPU opponents
- Character-select screen
- VS screen
- Arcade progression
- Training mode

### FKBC Streets

Side-scrolling beat-'em-up mode.

The player moves through scrolling environments fighting groups of opponents.

Features:

- Horizontal and vertical movement
- Walking depth within the stage
- Punch and kick combinations
- Running attacks
- Jump attacks
- Throws
- Knockdowns
- Pickups
- Breakable scenery
- Multiple enemies simultaneously
- Enemy waves
- Mini-bosses
- Coach boss battles
- Stage transitions
- Health pickups
- Score and combo system
- Continue system

The same core fighters and animation library should be reusable between both modes,
with additional animations where the beat-'em-up mode requires them.

## Characters

Production characters:

1. Joe
2. Jack
3. John
4. Justin
5. Paul

Paul is the final arcade boss.

## Technical direction

- Phaser
- TypeScript
- 60 FPS
- Fixed logical game resolution
- Responsive scaling without geometry drift
- Landscape-first gameplay
- Touch virtual controller
- Keyboard support
- Physical game-controller support
- Capacitor for native iOS packaging
- GitHub source control
- Cloud iOS build pipeline
- TestFlight distribution

## Visual direction

Original FKBC artwork inspired by late 1980s / early 1990s console and arcade games.

Do not use copyrighted Street Fighter, Mortal Kombat or Streets of Rage characters,
sprites, logos, music, stages or other proprietary assets.

Target presentation:

- SNES / Mega Drive-era arcade aesthetic
- Large readable fighters
- Detailed frame animation
- Strong impact animation
- Character-specific celebrations
- Arcade character-select presentation
- Retro console menus
- High-quality modern rendering of classic game design

## Development rule

Gameplay quality comes before quantity.

First production milestone:

Joe vs training opponent with complete movement, animation, collision, combat,
sound and controller systems.

Only expand to the other characters and FKBC Streets mode after the fundamental
combat system feels correct.
